{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":17378,"duration_api_ms":18729,"num_turns":5,"result":"I wrote the script to `src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. My sandbox blocked the `bpftrace` calls, including a dry run for a syntax check.\n\nIt attaches to the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint, which fires each time a CPU's frequency changes. For each change it prints the time since start, the CPU, the new frequency in MHz and the previous one. Press Ctrl-C to end the trace. It then prints a per-CPU histogram of frequencies and a per-CPU count of changes.\n\nThe previous frequency shows 0 for the first event on each CPU, because there's nothing earlier to compare against.\n\nTo run it:\n```bash\nsudo bpftrace src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt\n```\n\nThe tracepoint only fires if the system uses a cpufreq driver. On some VMs and on drivers that set frequency in hardware, you may see no events.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"87a80786-42aa-4113-b99c-239593343bda","total_cost_usd":0.0719785,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1770,"cache_read_input_tokens":128830,"output_tokens":1747,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1770},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":26727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":324,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":1747,"cacheReadInputTokens":128830,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1770,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0715275,"contextWin